{"name":"Mud Pack","hex":"#9d9588","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mud","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Mednyj Aleut."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mixture of water and soil or fine grained sediment.","A plaster-like mixture used to texture or smooth drywall."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mud"},{"term":"pack","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bundle made up and prepared to be carried; especially, a bundle to be carried on the back, but also a load for an animal, a bale.","A number or quantity equal to the contents of a pack"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put or bring things together in a limited or confined space, especially for storage or transport.\n To make a pack of; to arrange closely and securely in a pack; hence, to place and arrange compactly as in a pack","To make a pack of; to arrange closely and securely in a pack; hence, to place and arrange compactly as in a pack"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pack"}],"entries":[{"title":"List of teams and organizations in DC Comics","blocks":[{"text":"This is a list of teams and organizations that appear in various DC Comics publications."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_teams_and_organizations_in_DC_Comics"},{"title":"Mud","blocks":[{"text":"Mud is loam, silt, or clay mixed with water. Mud is usually formed after rainfall or near water sources. Ancient mud deposits hardened over geological time to form sedimentary rock such as shale or mudstone. When geological deposits of mud are formed in estuaries, the resultant layers are termed bay muds. Mud has also been used for centuries as a construction resource, mostly for houses, and also as a binder. An Old English word for it was fen, now in most dialects referring to a type of wetland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/2003-11-27_Northerner_boots_in_mud.jpg/330px-2003-11-27_Northerner_b